details.image_prompt:
[
  "Shot with a Canon EOS R5, 85mm f/1.8 lens. The scene features two plates, each holding two halved whole-wheat pita pockets positioned in a 3/4 overhead view to showcase the generous, textured filling. The pitas are slightly angled, revealing layers of dark green, fresh baby spinach at the base, topped with a creamy, pale yellow curried chicken salad mixture. Inside the salad, one can clearly identify chunks of crisp, ivory-colored Fuji apple, bright green diced celery, and earthy, rustic walnut pieces coated in a light, spiced yogurt dressing. The camera angle is 35-45 degrees, capturing the volume of the filling without hiding the ingredients. The background includes a second plate slightly blurred, emphasizing a realistic serving for two. Soft natural side light from a window to the left highlights the glistening, moist texture of the yogurt dressing and the crispness of the apple. The plates rest on an aged, rustic wooden surface with visible grain. Props include a small wooden spoon resting near a plate, a few stray walnut fragments, and a single vibrant spinach leaf on the table. Photorealistic, not AI-generated looking. The scene feels lived-in and authentic, captured just after preparation. Slight natural imperfections include an uneven crumb edge on the pita, a tiny drop of curry-tinted yogurt on the plate rim, and a scattered crumb trail. Warm, golden-hour color temperature. No plastic sheen, no artificial symmetry, no hands, no text, no logos. Indistinguishable from professional cookbook editorial photography."
]
